  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency winter food assistance (in-kind and cash-based transfers) to acutely food insecure people living in IPC Phase 3+</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of WFP project is to provide life-saving emergency food assistance to vulnerable households during the winter lean season. This project provides procurement of food and dispatch to relevant cooperating partners, as well as coordination with relevant line directorates at the provincial level, among other activities. The project provides life-saving assistance to 220,884 people, including 51,908 women, 50,803 men, 118,173 children, and 44,178 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
